// Adaptive Sorting Algorithm Implementation
// This program implements a sorting algorithm that can be evolved to adapt to different data patterns

use std::cmp::Ordering;

// EVOLVE-BLOCK-START
// HYPOTHESIS-1: A compact hybrid introsort with insertion sort for small subarrays and median-of-three pivot will improve performance_score by avoiding worst-case quicksort behavior
// MECHANISM-1: Median-of-three prevents O(n²) on sorted inputs; insertion sort is faster for small n; depth limit prevents stack overflow
// EXPECT-1: performance_score > 0.99
// RESULT-1: CONFIRMED (actual=0.9985544247130845)
// HYPOTHESIS-2: Reducing code size by removing unused is_nearly_sorted and merging into a single recursive function will improve fitness by satisfying the simplification hint
